Package: acrpdf
Version: @VERSION@
Section: office
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= @PY@), python3 (<< @PYNEXT@), libxcb-cursor0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, fontconfig, ghostscript, cups-client, libnss3-tools, xdg-utils
Recommends: cups, cups-filters, libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, libreoffice-impress, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-spa, tesseract-ocr-eng, sane-utils, gnome-keyring, fonts-dejavu-core
Suggests: google-chrome-stable | chromium
Conflicts: lumenpdf
Replaces: lumenpdf
Maintainer: Felipe Mogro <felipemogro@hotmail.com>
Description: open-source alternative to Adobe Acrobat with iLovePDF-style tools
 AcrPDF views, annotates and edits PDF files; fills and creates forms;
 signs with handwritten signatures (draw, type, PNG or SVG) and with digital
 certificates (PAdES, .p12/.pfx files or the Firefox certificate store);
 stamps, organizes, merges, splits, compresses, converts (Word, Excel,
 PowerPoint, images, HTML, Markdown, PDF/A), protects, redacts and hides
 Spanish ID numbers (DNI/NIE).
 .
 It also installs the "AcrPDF" virtual printer (CUPS) that saves PDF files in
 ~/PDF. Optional AI summaries and translations use the Claude API or a local
 Ollama model.
